# A SQL query with WHERE, GROUP BY, ORDER BY and LIMIT gets a rewrite of every clause.
mode: syntax
---- query
SELECT customerId, SUM(amount) AS total FROM t WHERE amount > 0 GROUP BY customerId ORDER BY total DESC LIMIT 3
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..112
  PIPELINE@0..111
    ERROR@0..111
      IDENT@0..6 "SELECT"
      WHITESPACE@6..7 " "
      IDENT@7..17 "customerId"
      COMMA@17..18 ","
      WHITESPACE@18..19 " "
      IDENT@19..22 "SUM"
      L_PAREN@22..23 "("
      IDENT@23..29 "amount"
      R_PAREN@29..30 ")"
      WHITESPACE@30..31 " "
      IDENT@31..33 "AS"
      WHITESPACE@33..34 " "
      IDENT@34..39 "total"
      WHITESPACE@39..40 " "
      IDENT@40..44 "FROM"
      WHITESPACE@44..45 " "
      IDENT@45..46 "t"
      WHITESPACE@46..47 " "
      IDENT@47..52 "WHERE"
      WHITESPACE@52..53 " "
      IDENT@53..59 "amount"
      WHITESPACE@59..60 " "
      GT@60..61 ">"
      WHITESPACE@61..62 " "
      LONG@62..63 "0"
      WHITESPACE@63..64 " "
      IDENT@64..69 "GROUP"
      WHITESPACE@69..70 " "
      IDENT@70..72 "BY"
      WHITESPACE@72..73 " "
      IDENT@73..83 "customerId"
      WHITESPACE@83..84 " "
      IDENT@84..89 "ORDER"
      WHITESPACE@89..90 " "
      IDENT@90..92 "BY"
      WHITESPACE@92..93 " "
      IDENT@93..98 "total"
      WHITESPACE@98..99 " "
      IDENT@99..103 "DESC"
      WHITESPACE@103..104 " "
      IDENT@104..109 "LIMIT"
      WHITESPACE@109..110 " "
      LONG@110..111 "3"
  WHITESPACE@111..112 "\n"

error[DS0105]: `SELECT ... FROM` is SQL, not DataScript
  --> query:1:1
  |
1 | SELECT customerId, SUM(amount) AS total FROM t WHERE amount > 0 GROUP BY customerId ORDER BY total DESC LIMIT 3
  | ^^^^^^                                  ---- in DataScript the table comes first
  | |
  | this is SQL
  |
  = help: start with the table and pipe it into operators: `from t | where amount > 0 | summarize total = sum(amount) by customerId | sort by total desc | take 3`
